    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d173">

                <pb facs="0441" n="345" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg345"/>

                <head>No. 171.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Mr. Williams.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-09-12"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 12,
                        1874</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 186.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your dispatch of July 7, No.
                    44, relating to the joint trial at Ohifu of persons who attacked Mr. Corbett, an
                    American missionary <pb facs="0442" n="346" xml:id="pg346"/> at Chimi, I take
                    pleasure in stating that your course in relation to the matter is regarded by
                    the Department as prudent and fair, and that Mr. Sheppard has the cordial
                    approval of the Department for the firmness and discretion displayed by him in
                    conducting the case.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
